pierre/test/DiffHunksRendererVirtualization.test.ts|expandHunk(3, 'both', Infinity)|a large finite count (usize has no infinity)
pierre/test/patchFileRender.test.ts|patch digest and rendered-row snapshots|replaced by: one hunk, column line counts equal the hunk's counts, every rendered line is a patch line
pierre/test/InjectedRowHooks.test.ts|UnresolvedFileHunksRenderer emits merge conflict action rows inline|deferred with the merge-conflict renderer
pierre/test/renderTokenLines.test.ts|undecorated editor lines retain whitespace positions and empty-line placeholders|drives useTokenTransformer (editor token transformer), not ported
pierre/test/DiffHunksRendererLanguages.test.ts|the bundled Terraform loader renders an ordinary .tf edit and provides its aliases|hasLoadedLanguages is `not disposed` for the bundled lexers; the aliases are checked against the highlights language table
pierre/test/DiffHunksRendererLanguages.test.ts|asyncRender <lang> -> <lang>, cold/destination loaded (8 cases)|lazy grammar loading does not exist for the highlights backend; the four language pairs are one test each, asserting the grammars used by both sides
pierre/test/DiffHunksRendererLanguages.test.ts|renderDiff loads the missing source grammar / hydrate preloads both grammars (4 cases)|async background loading, hydrate and onRenderUpdate are dropped (PARITY.md dropped branches)
pierre/test/UniversalRenderingManager.test.ts|all cases|the module-level queue is a `UniversalRenderingManager` over `FakeFrames`; bun `mock()` is a call log of the times received
pierre/test/Virtualizer.reconcileQueue.test.ts|requestHeightReconcile reconciles instances the pass did not repaint|jsdom root/content/container are FakeHost elements; `await wait(20)` flushes the fake frame queue
pierre/test/Virtualizer.scrollState.test.ts|reads and restores an element / document root logical scroll position|jsdom `scrollTo` stubs and `window.scrollY` / `innerHeight` overrides are the FakeHost world; its `scrollTo` clamps to the scrollable range as a browser does (no assertion can tell: every target is in range or already clamped by the virtualizer); `toEqual` on recorded scroll calls compares the host trace
pierre/test/InteractionManager.gutterUtility.test.ts|all 17 tests of `InteractionManager gutter utility`|jsdom is the FakeDom model; `dispatchPointer` routes to the `pre` handlers then the document handlers and returns `defaultPrevented`; `setElementFromPoint` is the fake's hit table; `querySelector('[data-gutter-utility-slot]')` is `has_descendant`
pierre/test/InteractionManager.gutterUtility.test.ts|InteractionManager editor active-line state (6 tests)|dropped with the editor active line (edit mode is OUT)
pierre/src/utils/areOptionsEqual.ts|`areObjectsEqual(optionsA, optionsB, ['theme','parseDiffOptions'])` key-by-key identity|derived field-wise equality (see the header); callbacks by `Rc` pointer, which is JavaScript's identity comparison of functions
pierre/test/FileDiff.partialHydration.test.ts|the converted tests (expandHunk hydrates once, expandHunk without a loader throws, added or deleted partial diffs, ignores loaded files if the source is already full, the synthetic bottom hunk, expandHunk on full diffs, partial after full, hydrate twice, hydrate after render, stale loader results, hydrated cache keys x2, pure rename, loader errors and retry)|`loadDiffFiles` is host-driven: `LoaderHarness` is the host (`poll` starts one load per pending request, `resolve` is `deferred.resolve` and calls `files_loaded`, `reject` is a failed load and calls `abandon_file_load`); `waitForHydrated` and the awaits are gone (synchronous); `expect(getInputDiff()).toBe(partial)` after a hydration is the instance reading back the hydrated `Rc` (the old `Rc` stays partial, see `loading.rs`); `toThrow` is a `catch_unwind` panic-message check; `__prepareForEditing`/`prepareForEditing` assertions are dropped (edit mode); `partial.isPartial = false` is a copy with the flag cleared; `console.error` of a loader failure is the host's
pierre/test/FileDiff.partialHydration.test.ts|a new edit waits for its external baseline before creating a keyless session; a full replacement can start editing before the old partial load completes; recycle reuses an in-flight load before the editor attaches; the first edit after pure-rename hydration separates the aliased file sides|edit session (edit mode is OUT)
pierre/test/FileDiff.partialHydration.test.ts|primes eligible worker highlights with the hydrated source diff; continues after the worker priming timeout elapses; commits hydrated diffs when worker priming rejects; ignores stale hydration results after the rendered diff changes while priming is pending|worker pool and async highlight cache (OUT)
pierre/test/FileDiff.partialHydration.test.ts|rejects the hydration promise when disableErrorHandling is true|the hydration promise and `disableErrorHandling` do not exist: loading is host-driven and a failed load is the host's (`abandon_file_load`, covered by the loader errors test)
pierre/test/themeTypeUpdates.test.ts|FileDiff.setThemeType applies paired themeType changes immediately; FileDiff.render applies themeType changes during partial renders|`DEFAULT_THEMES` over the plain-text stub highlighter (the style text's `color-scheme` comes from the CSS wrapper, not the highlighter); `waitForThemeScheme` is a synchronous query of `style[data-theme-css]` and the test also asserts the style element is the same one throughout
pierre/test/themeTypeUpdates.test.ts|CodeView applies paired themeType changes on the next render tick; CodeView-owned virtualized items reject direct themeType changes|CodeView and `VirtualizedFile` (OUT / S12b)
pierre/test/themeTypeUpdates.test.ts|File.setThemeType applies paired themeType changes immediately; File.render applies themeType changes during partial renders|`File` (single-file view) is DEFER
pierre/test/virtualizedFileDiffEstimatedHeights.test.ts|computes split and unified estimates together on first prepare / reserves synthetic bottom separator height for hydratable partial diffs / recomputes estimates when file loader availability changes / keeps estimates and measurements for an equivalent diff cache key / clears estimates and measurements for changed diff content|ported over `LayoutInstance` (test-only: the instance around `DiffLayout`): `instance.updateCodeViewLayout(diff, 0)` (the CodeView layout pass, not ported) is `LayoutInstance::update_layout`, its layout half (`layoutDiffChanged` via `areDiffTargetsEqual`, the cache resets, `computeApproximateSize`); `setOptions` is `LayoutInstance::set_options` (the layout half: `hasDiffLayoutOptionChanged`, `hasDiffEstimateOptionChanged`, `resetLayoutCache`); `getVirtualizedHeight()` is `layout.height`; `loadDiffFiles` is `has_diff_file_loader`; the huge single-block diff is upstream's literal as JSON
pierre/test/virtualFileMetricsPadding.test.ts|VirtualizedFileDiff: uses paddingBottom instead of spacing in total height / does not add paddingBottom when a diff has no hunks|ported over `LayoutInstance` like the estimated-heights cases (`updateCodeViewLayout(diff, 0)` is `update_layout`, `getVirtualizedHeight()` is `layout.height`); `baseMetrics` is the partial metrics struct
pierre/src/components/FileDiff.ts|render with no rows: after `pre.remove(); this.pre = void 0` upstream leaves `codeDeletions`/`codeAdditions`/`codeUnified` pointing at the detached rows|the port discards those rows (a `pre` this render made itself at the end of the render, an older one after the next manager setup), so the references are cleared with `pre`; found by the S12b-2 churn test (an empty render queued one retired node per call and, once freed, `reconcileHeights` would have read freed rows)
pierre/src/components/VirtualizedFileDiff.ts|`render` without a diff: `console.error` and `return false`|panics (a render before the instance was given anything is a programming error)
pierre/src/components/VirtualizedFileDiff.ts|`handleFilesLoaded`'s in-place `hydratePartialDiff('merge')`|the hydrated diff is a new `Rc`: the instance swaps it for the old one in its input, rendered and pending data and in `pendingRender`, as upstream's one mutated object is seen everywhere
pierre/src/components/Virtualizer.ts|`scrollFix`: `scrollTo({ top: scrollTop + offset, behavior: 'instant' })` reads `scrollTop` synchronously|the element branch calls the host method `element_scroll_by(root, offset)`, whose default is upstream's read-then-write; the Dioxus host (pierre_diffs_dioxus) overrides it to `get_scroll_offset().await` then `scroll(offset + delta)` in one spawned task, because standard Dioxus can only read a scroll offset asynchronously and the last `onscroll` value is stale by the scrolls still in flight (the W2 spike measured a 50 px jump from the stale value, none from read-then-scroll). The window (document) branch is unchanged
pierre/src/managers/InteractionManager.ts|`pre.addEventListener('click' | 'pointerdown' | 'pointermove' | 'pointerleave')` with `event.composedPath()` / `event.target`|the Dioxus host (pierre_diffs_dioxus) cannot read an event's target, only which element's handler runs, so it attaches the handlers to the nodes the manager resolves targets from (the `pre`, lines, line numbers, expand controls, utility and annotation wrappers) and each reports its own node key; the manager walks up from it as it walks `composedPath()`. One event that bubbles through several of them is delivered once, from the innermost (the same payload `Rc` reaches all handlers). Nodes below such a node (tokens) report their line, which `resolvePointerTarget` reaches anyway because token interactions are dropped. A view whose options give rows nothing to do (hunk expansion only) attaches only the expand and `pre` click handlers. `pointerover`/`pointerout` are not used by the manager and are not wired
pierre/src/managers/InteractionManager.ts|`document.addEventListener('pointermove' | 'pointerup' | 'pointercancel')` during a drag|standard Dioxus has no document listener, so `add_document_listeners` sets a host flag and the view's top node renders the three handlers, which forward only while the flag is set. Moves that hit a row's handler reach the manager with that row as target; up and cancel reach it with no target (the manager reads a target only for the event-path fallback of a move and the gutter drag's end). A mouse `pointermove` with no button held while a drag is active is delivered as the `pointerup` that happened where no event reaches the view (outside its window), because a drag the manager still holds waits for it and ignores every later `pointerdown`; touch and pen release inside the view (implicit capture) and are not read this way. Dispatch outside the top node (a drag leaving the view) is not seen until the pointer re-enters
pierre/src/managers/InteractionManager.ts|`document.elementFromPoint(x, y)` / `shadowRoot.elementFromPoint`|the Dioxus host answers from its cached row geometry: when a drag starts it asks the engine for the client rects of the `pre` and of one content column (async `get_client_rect`), which anchor the stacked row heights it already keeps (`onresize`); a lookup moves the anchor by the scroll and layout shift since. It answers the content-column child (line, annotation, buffer) under the point and not the gutter cell, which the manager normalizes to the row; a split diff's two columns share the pre equally (the stylesheet's `1fr 1fr`). A non-virtualized view measures its rows the same way (`onresize` on each line, annotation and no-newline row, and `onmounted` on the `pre` and a content column) while the pointer acts on rows, which costs one resize listener per row and suits short diffs (every view also measures hunk separators, into the geometry cache only, since no style sets a separator's height and the rows below one would sit off by it; heights are border boxes, so the stylesheet's block margin around a hunk separator, which no event reports, is read at drag start from the client rects of each separator and the row after it and added to the stack, or every separator above a point would make the drag resolve rows below the pointer); with no scroller its scroll position is 0 and the rect measured at drag start is the whole anchor. Until the rects land, or on a renderer without client rects, it answers `Unavailable` and the manager follows the event path (a mouse drag still works; a touch drag stays on its origin row)
pierre/src/managers/InteractionManager.ts|`handlePointerClick(event: MouseEvent)` reading `event.pointerId`/`pointerType`|`click` arrives as the platform's mouse payload (no pointer id or type); the manager reads only the target and shift key of a click, so the host fills pointer id 0 and type mouse
pierre/src/managers/InteractionManager.ts|`hoveredLine` / `gutterUtilityLine` kept as references to elements a render replaced|upstream leaves them pointing at detached elements (the utility container is appended into the detached number element, out of the view, and `getHoveredLine` keeps answering the replaced row's line); the owner here frees replaced rows after the manager's `setup`, and the container with them, so `setup` ends both while the rows exist: the hover is cleared and the utility hidden (the container is out of any row, as upstream's detached placement has it), and `getHoveredLine` answers no line until the pointer moves
